{"id":"G0114","name":"Chimera","aliases":[],"url":"https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0114","summary":"Chimera is a suspected China-based threat group that has been active since at least 2018 targeting the semiconductor industry in Taiwan as well as data from the airline industry.","summaryCites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"},{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}],"procedures":[{"id":"T1027.010","text":"Chimera has encoded PowerShell commands.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1036.005","text":"Chimera has renamed malware to GoogleUpdate.exe and WinRAR to jucheck.exe, RecordedTV.ms, teredo.tmp, update.exe, and msadcs1.exe.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1070.004","text":"Chimera has performed file deletion to evade detection.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1070.006","text":"Chimera has used a Windows version of the Linux `touch` command to modify the date and time stamp on DLLs.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1078","text":"Chimera has used a valid account to maintain persistence via scheduled task.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1078.002","text":"Chimera has used compromised domain accounts to gain access to the target environment.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1556.001","text":"Chimera's malware has altered the NTLM authentication program on domain controllers to allow Chimera to login without a valid credential.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1574.001","text":"Chimera has used side loading to place malicious DLLs in memory.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1685.005","text":"Chimera has cleared event logs on compromised hosts.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1589.001","text":"Chimera has collected credentials for the target organization from previous breaches for use in brute force attacks.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1588.002","text":"Chimera has obtained and used tools such as BloodHound, Cobalt Strike, Mimikatz, and PsExec.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"},{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1133","text":"Chimera has used legitimate credentials to login to an external VPN, Citrix, SSH, and other remote services.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"},{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1047","text":"Chimera has used WMIC to execute remote commands.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"},{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1053.005","text":"Chimera has used scheduled tasks to invoke Cobalt Strike including through batch script `schtasks /create /ru \"SYSTEM\" /tn \"update\" /tr \"cmd /c c:\\windows\\temp\\update.bat\" /sc once /f /st` and to maintain persistence.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"},{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1059.001","text":"Chimera has used PowerShell scripts to execute malicious payloads and the DSInternals PowerShell module to make use of Active Directory features.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"},{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1059.003","text":"Chimera has used the Windows Command Shell and batch scripts for execution on compromised hosts.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1106","text":"Chimera has used direct Windows system calls by leveraging Dumpert.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1569.002","text":"Chimera has used PsExec to deploy beacons on compromised systems.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1003.003","text":"Chimera has gathered the SYSTEM registry and ntds.dit files from target systems. Chimera specifically has used the NtdsAudit tool to dump the password hashes of domain users via `msadcs.exe \"NTDS.dit\" -s \"SYSTEM\" -p RecordedTV_pdmp.txt --users-csv RecordedTV_users.csv` and used ntdsutil to copy the Active Directory database.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"},{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1110.003","text":"Chimera has used multiple password spraying attacks against victim's remote services to obtain valid user and administrator accounts.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1110.004","text":"Chimera has used credential stuffing against victim's remote services to obtain valid accounts.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1111","text":"Chimera has registered alternate phone numbers for compromised users to intercept 2FA codes sent via SMS.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1007","text":"Chimera has used `net start` and `net use` for system service discovery.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1012","text":"Chimera has queried Registry keys using `reg query \\\\<host>\\HKU\\<SID>\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Terminal Server Client\\Servers` and `reg query \\\\<host>\\HKU\\<SID>\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings`.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1016","text":"Chimera has used ipconfig, Ping, and `tracert` to enumerate the IP address and network environment and settings of the local host.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1018","text":"Chimera has utilized various scans and queries to find domain controllers and remote services in the target environment.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1033","text":"Chimera has used the `quser` command to show currently logged on users.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1046","text":"Chimera has used the `get -b <start ip> -e <end ip> -p` command for network scanning as well as a custom Python tool packed into a Windows executable named Get.exe to scan IP ranges for HTTP.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1049","text":"Chimera has used `netstat -ano | findstr EST` to discover network connections.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1057","text":"Chimera has used `tasklist` to enumerate processes.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1069.001","text":"Chimera has used `net localgroup administrators` to identify accounts with local administrative rights.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1083","text":"Chimera has utilized multiple commands to identify data of interest in file and directory listings.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1087.001","text":"Chimera has used `net user` for account discovery.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1087.002","text":"Chimera has has used `net user /dom` and `net user Administrator` to enumerate domain accounts including administrator accounts.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"},{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1124","text":"Chimera has used `time /t` and `net time \\\\ip/hostname` for system time discovery.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1135","text":"Chimera has used `net share` and `net view` to identify network shares of interest.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1201","text":"Chimera has used the NtdsAudit utility to collect information related to accounts and passwords.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1217","text":"Chimera has used `type \\\\<hostname>\\c$\\Users\\<username>\\Favorites\\Links\\Bookmarks bar\\Imported From IE\\*citrix*` for bookmark discovery.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1482","text":"Chimera has `nltest /domain_trusts` to identify domain trust relationships.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1680","text":"Chimera has used `fsutil fsinfo drives`, `systeminfo`, and `vssadmin list shadows` for system information including shadow volumes and drive information.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1021.001","text":"Chimera has used RDP to access targeted systems.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1021.002","text":"Chimera has used Windows admin shares to move laterally.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"},{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1021.006","text":"Chimera has used WinRM for lateral movement.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1550.002","text":"Chimera has dumped password hashes for use in pass the hash authentication attacks.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1570","text":"Chimera has copied tools between compromised hosts using SMB.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1039","text":"Chimera has collected data of interest from network shares.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1074.001","text":"Chimera has staged stolen data locally on compromised hosts.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1074.002","text":"Chimera has staged stolen data on designated servers in the target environment.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1114.001","text":"Chimera has harvested data from victim's e-mail including through execution of `wmic /node:<ip> process call create \"cmd /c copy c:\\Users\\<username>\\<path>\\backup.pst c:\\windows\\temp\\backup.pst\" copy \"i:\\<path>\\<username>\\My Documents\\<filename>.pst\" copy`.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1114.002","text":"Chimera has harvested data from remote mailboxes including through execution of `\\\\<hostname>\\c$\\Users\\<username>\\AppData\\Local\\Microsoft\\Outlook*.ost`.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1119","text":"Chimera has used custom DLLs for continuous retrieval of data from memory.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1213.002","text":"Chimera has collected documents from the victim's SharePoint.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1560.001","text":"Chimera has used gzip for Linux OS and a modified RAR software to archive data on Windows hosts.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"},{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1071.001","text":"Chimera has used HTTPS for C2 communications.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1071.004","text":"Chimera has used Cobalt Strike to encapsulate C2 in DNS traffic.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1105","text":"Chimera has remotely copied tools and malware onto targeted systems.","cites":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1572","text":"Chimera has encapsulated Cobalt Strike's C2 protocol in DNS and HTTPS.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1041","text":"Chimera has used Cobalt Strike C2 beacons for data exfiltration.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]},{"id":"T1567.002","text":"Chimera has exfiltrated stolen data to OneDrive accounts.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/"}]}],"observables":[{"kind":"file","value":"update.bat","tech":"T1053.005"},{"kind":"file","value":"msadcs.exe","tech":"T1003.003"},{"kind":"file","value":"GoogleUpdate.exe","tech":"T1036.005"},{"kind":"file","value":"jucheck.exe","tech":"T1036.005"},{"kind":"file","value":"update.exe","tech":"T1036.005"},{"kind":"file","value":"msadcs1.exe","tech":"T1036.005"},{"kind":"file","value":"Get.exe","tech":"T1046"},{"kind":"path","value":"\\\\<hostname>\\c$\\Users\\<username>\\AppData\\Local\\Microsoft\\Outlook*.ost","tech":"T1114.002"},{"kind":"command","value":"schtasks /create /ru \"SYSTEM\" /tn \"update\" /tr \"cmd /c c:\\windows\\temp\\update.bat\" /sc once /f /st","tech":"T1053.005"},{"kind":"command","value":"net user /dom","tech":"T1087.002"},{"kind":"command","value":"msadcs.exe \"NTDS.dit\" -s \"SYSTEM\" -p RecordedTV_pdmp.txt --users-csv RecordedTV_users.csv","tech":"T1003.003"},{"kind":"command","value":"get -b <start ip> -e <end ip> -p","tech":"T1046"},{"kind":"command","value":"time /t","tech":"T1124"},{"kind":"command","value":"netstat -ano | findstr EST","tech":"T1049"},{"kind":"lolbin","value":"tasklist","tech":"T1057"},{"kind":"lolbin","value":"tracert","tech":"T1016"},{"kind":"lolbin","value":"quser","tech":"T1033"},{"kind":"lolbin","value":"systeminfo","tech":"T1680"}],"sources":[{"name":"Cycraft Chimera April 2020","url":"https://cycraft.com/download/CyCraft-Whitepaper-Chimera_V4.1.pdf","desc":"Cycraft. (2020, April 15). APT Group Chimera - APT Operation Skeleton key Targets Taiwan Semiconductor Vendors. Retrieved August 24, 2020.."},{"name":"NCC Group Chimera January 2021","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230218064220/https://research.nccgroup.com/2021/01/12/abusing-cloud-services-to-fly-under-the-radar/","desc":"Jansen, W . (2021, January 12). Abusing cloud services to fly under the radar. Retrieved September 12, 2024."}],"softwareLinks":[{"id":"S0521","n":"BloodHound","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0521/"},{"id":"S0154","n":"Cobalt Strike","t":"malware","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0154/"},{"id":"S0404","n":"esentutl","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0404/"},{"id":"S0002","n":"Mimikatz","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0002/"},{"id":"S0039","n":"Net","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0039/"},{"id":"S0029","n":"PsExec","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0029/"}]}